# The -2 with two creatures each. Players choose in turn order, the active player (Bot1, Garruk's controller) first: Bot1 chooses its
# Elvish Mystic (not the Ornithopter, the first offered), then Bot2 its Ornithopter (not the Mystic, the first offered). If the
# order were reversed each line would meet the other player's question and the defaults would sacrifice the wrong creatures.
# "If you sacrificed a creature this way": Bot1 did, and gets the Beast. Bot2's Ornithopter is exiled (an opponent's creature
# that would die), Bot1's Mystic goes to the graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Garruk, Veiled Butcher
Ornithopter
Elvish Mystic
Forest
Forest x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Elvish Mystic
Ornithopter
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Garruk, Veiled Butcher.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Garruk, Veiled Butcher.Activate(Ability: Each player sacrifices)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Elvish Mystic)
Bot2.Choose(Ornithopter)
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Beast Token; Forest; Garruk, Veiled Butcher; Mox Jet; Mox Jet; Ornithopter
Bot1.Graveyard = Elvish Mystic; Black Lotus
Bot2.Battlefield = Elvish Mystic; Mox Emerald
Exile = Ornithopter
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Garruk, Veiled Butcher.Counters.Loyalty = 3
